From 566ee5f588fa85bda441c20844572742224f3d3f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sambukuper <sambukuper@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 22:02:31 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Add horizon-steam: e4steam's Steam friends multiplayer,
 ported

e4steam is a Java mod (Fabric/Forge/NeoForge); Java jars do not run on
Horizon, so what the mod does arrives natively: the host's world opens to
a Steam lobby (friends join freely, or only by invitation), guests
connect over Steam's P2P networking sockets on the mod's own virtual
port 480, and each session is pumped byte for byte to the integrated
server's LAN port, as Play with Friends carries its invite-code
sessions. App ID 480 is the mod's, and so is the identity scheme: a
guest logs in as s_<steamid in base 36> with the UUID the mod derives
from the SteamID, and the host's tunnel checks the login name against
the Steam connection's identity before a byte reaches the server. The
lobby's metadata (protocol, game, host) keeps foreign App ID 480 traffic
out, as the mod filters its own.

cargo test -p horizon-steam covers what needs no Steam: the identity
derivation against vectors computed from the Java algorithm, the
safe-name round trip, address parsing, and the opening check (a real
handshake and Hello arriving in pieces, wrong names, a status ping,
garbage).

Co-Authored-By: ZCode (GLM-5.3-Flash) <noreply@z.ai>
