From cf4e2cea1c972450dc90501b5b9f8d0a69068180 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sambukuper <sambukuper@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 22:03:22 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Open the world to Steam friends from Play with Friends
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The screen's Steam section (there when Steam is signed in) offers Open to
Steam Friends and Invitation Only, Copy Address, Invite Friends through
the overlay's invite dialog, and Stop. Starting it opens the world to LAN
as invite-code sharing does, and the two shares hand the LAN port over to
each other instead of closing it under the other's guests. Guests join
from a Steam invitation (accepting one at the title screen joins the
lobby the callback names) or the world's steam:<lobby id> address —
Direct Connection takes a bare lobby id too — and log in under their own
Steam account's safe name, which the host's check expects. Without the
client's `steam` feature nothing is offered and nothing links: the
section is absent and steam: addresses report that the build lacks it.

Co-Authored-By: ZCode (GLM-5.3-Flash) <noreply@z.ai>
